# MCP/tool boundaries

An MCP server grants technical capability, not institutional authority.

- Use only MCP servers relevant to the mission.
- Do not broaden scope because a tool is available.
- Never place raw secrets in committed `.cursor/mcp.json`.
- Prefer OAuth or environment-variable interpolation.
- Do not use external tools to mutate canon, production, credentials, permissions, billing, or protected data unless explicitly authorized.
- Record material external actions in the run return.
